 href=\"#cite_note-Kuster-30\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>28<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"New Jersey03&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/New_Jersey%27s_3rd_congressional_district\" title=\"New Jersey&#39;s 3rd congressional district\">New Jersey&#160;3</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Andy_Kim_(politician)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Andy Kim (politician)\">Andy Kim</a> retired to <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_New_Jersey\" title=\"2024 United States Senate election in New Jersey\">run for the U.S. Senate</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-KimNJ&#95;31-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-KimNJ-31\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>29<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"North Carolina06&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/North_Carolina%27s_6th_congressional_district\" title=\"North Carolina&#39;s 6th congressional district\">North Carolina&#160;6</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Kathy_Manning\" title=\"Kathy Manning\">Kathy Manning</a> retired due to redistricting.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-manning&#95;32-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-manning-32\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>30<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"North Carolina13&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/North_Carolina%27s_13th_congressional_district\" title=\"North Carolina&#39;s 13th congressional district\">North Carolina&#160;13</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Wiley_Nickel\" title=\"Wiley Nickel\">Wiley Nickel</a> retired due to redistricting.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-WileyNC&#95;33-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-WileyNC-33\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>31<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"North Carolina14&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/North_Carolina%27s_14th_congressional_district\" title=\"North Carolina&#39;s 14th congressional district\">North Carolina&#160;14</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Jeff_Jackson_(politician)\" title=\"Jeff Jackson (politician)\">Jeff Jackson</a> retired to <a href=\"/wiki/2024_North_Carolina_Attorney_General_election\" title=\"2024 North Carolina Attorney General election\">run for attorney general of North Carolina</a> due to redistricting.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-JacksonNC&#95;34-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-JacksonNC-34\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>32<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Northern Mariana IslandsAL&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Northern_Mariana_Islands%27_at-large_congressional_district\" title=\"Northern Mariana Islands&#39; at-large congressional district\">Northern Mariana Islands&#160;at-large</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Gregorio_Sablan\" title=\"Gregorio Sablan\">Gregorio Sablan</a> retired.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-Sablan&#95;35-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Sablan-35\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>33<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Oregon03&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Oregon%27s_3rd_congressional_district\" title=\"Oregon&#39;s 3rd congressional district\">Oregon&#160;3</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Earl_Blumenauer\" title=\"Earl Blumenauer\">Earl Blumenauer</a> retired.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-BlumenauerOR&#95;36-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-BlumenauerOR-36\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>34<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Texas32&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Texas%27s_32nd_congressional_district\" title=\"Texas&#39;s 32nd congressional district\">Texas&#160;32</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Colin_Allred\" title=\"Colin Allred\">Colin Allred</a> retired to <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Texas\" title=\"2024 United States Senate election in Texas\">run for the U.S. Senate</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-Allred&#95;37-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Allred-37\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>35<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Virginia%27s_7th_congressional_district\" title=\"Virginia&#39;s 7th congressional district\">Virginia 7</a>: <a href=\"/wiki/Abigail_Spanberger\" title=\"Abigail Spanberger\">Abigail Spanberger</a> retired to <a href=\"/wiki/2025_Virginia_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2025 Virginia gubernatorial election\">run for governor of Virginia</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-SpanbergerVA&#95;38-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SpanbergerVA-38\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>36<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Virginia10&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Virginia%27s_10th_congressional_district\" title=\"Virginia&#39;s 10th congressional district\">Virginia&#160;10</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Jennifer_Wexton\" title=\"Jennifer Wexton\">Jennifer Wexton</a> retired.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-WextonVA&#95;39-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-WextonVA-39\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>37<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li></ol>\n</div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Republican\">Republican</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Republican\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1184024115\" /><div class=\"div-col\">\n<ol><li><span data-sort-value=\"Arizona08&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Arizona%27s_8th_congressional_district\" title=\"Arizona&#39;s 8th congressional district\">Arizona&#160;8</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Debbie_Lesko\" title=\"Debbie Lesko\">Debbie Lesko</a> retired to <a href=\"/wiki/2024_Maricopa_County_Board_of_Supervisors_election#District_4\" title=\"2024 Maricopa County Board of Supervisors election\">run for the Maricopa County Board of Supervisors</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-Lesko&#95;40-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Lesko-40\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>38<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Colorado04&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Colorado%27s_4th_congressional_district\" title=\"Colorado&#39;s 4th congressional district\">Colorado&#160;4</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Greg_Lopez\" title=\"Greg Lopez\">Greg Lopez</a> retired.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-GregLopez&#95;41-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-GregLopez-41\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>39<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Colorado05&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Colorado%27s_5th_congressional_district\" title=\"Colorado&#39;s 5th congressional district\">Colorado&#160;5</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Doug_Lamborn\" title=\"Doug Lamborn\">Doug Lamborn</a> retired.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-LambornCO&#95;42-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-LambornCO-42\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>40<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Florida08&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Florida%27s_8th_congressional_district\" title=\"Florida&#39;s 8th congressional district\">Florida&#160;8</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Bill_Posey\" title=\"Bill Posey\">Bill Posey</a> retired.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-posey&#95;43-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-posey-43\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>41<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Georgia03&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Georgia%27s_3rd_congressional_district\" title=\"Georgia&#39;s 3rd congressional district\">Georgia&#160;3</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Drew_Ferguson_(politician)\" title=\"Drew Ferguson (politician)\">Drew F