ata-sort-value=\"North Carolina10&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/North_Carolina%27s_10th_congressional_district\" title=\"North Carolina&#39;s 10th congressional district\">North Carolina&#160;10</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Patrick_McHenry\" title=\"Patrick McHenry\">Patrick McHenry</a> retired.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-McHenry&#95;52-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-McHenry-52\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>50<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"North DakotaAL&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/North_Dakota%27s_at-large_congressional_district\" title=\"North Dakota&#39;s at-large congressional district\">North Dakota&#160;at-large</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Kelly_Armstrong\" title=\"Kelly Armstrong\">Kelly Armstrong</a> retired to <a href=\"/wiki/2024_North_Dakota_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2024 North Dakota gubernatorial election\">run for governor of North Dakota</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-Armstrong&#95;53-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Armstrong-53\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>51<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Ohio02&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Ohio%27s_2nd_congressional_district\" title=\"Ohio&#39;s 2nd congressional district\">Ohio&#160;2</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Brad_Wenstrup\" title=\"Brad Wenstrup\">Brad Wenstrup</a> retired.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-WenstrupOH&#95;54-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-WenstrupOH-54\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>52<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Puerto RicoAL&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Puerto_Rico%27s_at-large_congressional_district\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Puerto Rico&#39;s at-large congressional district\">Puerto Rico&#160;at-large</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Jenniffer_Gonz%C3%A1lez-Col%C3%B3n\" title=\"Jenniffer González-Colón\">Jenniffer González-Colón</a> retired to <a href=\"/wiki/2024_Puerto_Rico_gubernatorial_election\" title=\"2024 Puerto Rico gubernatorial election\">run for governor of Puerto Rico</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-GonzalezColon&#95;55-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-GonzalezColon-55\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>53<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"South Carolina03&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/South_Carolina%27s_3rd_congressional_district\" title=\"South Carolina&#39;s 3rd congressional district\">South Carolina&#160;3</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Jeff_Duncan_(politician)\" title=\"Jeff Duncan (politician)\">Jeff Duncan</a> retired.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-Duncan&#95;56-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Duncan-56\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>54<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Texas12&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Texas%27s_12th_congressional_district\" title=\"Texas&#39;s 12th congressional district\">Texas&#160;12</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Kay_Granger\" title=\"Kay Granger\">Kay Granger</a> retired.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-Granger&#95;57-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Granger-57\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>55<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Texas26&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Texas%27s_26th_congressional_district\" title=\"Texas&#39;s 26th congressional district\">Texas&#160;26</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Michael_C._Burgess\" title=\"Michael C. Burgess\">Michael C. Burgess</a> retired.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-Burgess&#95;58-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Burgess-58\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>56<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Utah03&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Utah%27s_3rd_congressional_district\" title=\"Utah&#39;s 3rd congressional district\">Utah&#160;3</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/John_Curtis\" title=\"John Curtis\">John Curtis</a> retired to <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Utah\" title=\"2024 United States Senate election in Utah\">run for the U.S. Senate</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-Curtis&#95;59-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Curtis-59\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>57<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Washington05&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Washington%27s_5th_congressional_district\" title=\"Washington&#39;s 5th congressional district\">Washington&#160;5</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Cathy_McMorris_Rodgers\" title=\"Cathy McMorris Rodgers\">Cathy McMorris Rodgers</a> retired.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-McMorrisRodgers&#95;60-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-McMorrisRodgers-60\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>58<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"West Virginia02&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/West_Virginia%27s_2nd_congressional_district\" title=\"West Virginia&#39;s 2nd congressional district\">West Virginia&#160;2</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Alex_Mooney\" title=\"Alex Mooney\">Alex Mooney</a> retired to <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_West_Virginia\" title=\"2024 United States Senate election in West Virginia\">run for the U.S. Senate</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-AlexMooney&#95;61-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-AlexMooney-61\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>59<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li></ol>\n</div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Resignation_and_deaths\">Resignation and deaths</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Resignation and deaths\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<p>Three seats were left vacant on the day of the general election due to resignation or deaths in 2024, one of which was not filled until the next Congress.\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Democratic_2\">Democratic</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Democratic\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<p>Two Democrats died in office.\n</p>\n<ol><li><span data-sort-value=\"New Jersey09&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/New_Jersey%27s_9th_congressional_district\" title=\"New Jersey&#39;s 9th congressional district\">New Jersey&#160;9</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Bill_Pascrell\" title=\"Bill Pascrell\">Bill Pascrell</a> died on August 21, 2024.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-Pascrell&#95;62-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Pascrell-62\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>60<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Texas18&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Texas%27s_18th_congressional_district\" title=\"Texas&#39;s 18th congressional district\">Texas&#160;18</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Sheila_Jackson_Lee\" title=\"Sheila Jackson Lee\">Sheila Jackson Lee</a> died on July 19, 2024.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-Lee&#95;63-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Lee-63\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>61<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> A <a href=\"/wiki/2024_Texas%27s_18th_congressional_district_special_election\" title=\"2024 Texas&#39;s 18th congressional district special election\">special election</a> to fill the remainder of her term was held concurrently with the general election for the next full term, won by <a href=\"/wiki/Erica_Lee_Carter\" title=\"Erica Lee Carter\">Erica Lee Carter</a>.</li></ol>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Republican_2\">Republican</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Republican\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<p>One Republican resigned before the end of the term.\n</p>\n<ol><li><span data-sort-value=\"Wisconsin08&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Wisconsin%27s_8th_congressional_district\" title=\"Wisconsin&#39;s 8th congressional district\">Wisconsin&#160;8</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Mike_Gallagher_(American_politician)\" title=\"Mike Gallagher (American politician)\">Mike Gallagher</a> resigned on April 24.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-Gallagher&#95;64-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Gallagher-64\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>62<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> A <a href=\"/wiki/2024_Wisconsin%27s_8th_congressional_district_special_election\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 Wisconsin&#39;s 8th congressional district special election\">special election</a> to fill the remainder of his term was held concurrently with the general election for the next full term, won by <a href=\"/wiki/Tony_Wied\" title=\"Tony Wied\">Tony Wied</a>.</li></ol>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Incumbents_defeated\">Incumbents defeated</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Incumbents defeated\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"In_primary_elections\">In primary elections</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: In primary elections\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Democratic_3\">Democratic</h4><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Democratic\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<p>Two Democrats lost renomination.\n</p>\n<ol><li><span data-sort-value=\"Missouri01&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Missouri%27s_1st_congressional_district\" title=\"Missouri&#39;s 1st congressional district\">Missouri&#160;1</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Cori_Bush\" title=\"Cori Bush\">Cori Bush</a> lost renomination to <a href=\"/wiki/Wesley_Bell\" title=\"Wesley Bell\">Wesley Bell</a>, who won the general election.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-CoriBush&#95;65-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-CoriBush-65\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>63<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"New York16&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/New_York%27s_16th_congressional_district\" title=\"New York&#39;s 16th congressional district\">New York&#160;16</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Jamaal_Bowman\" title=\"Jamaal Bowman\">Jamaal Bowman</a> lost renomination to <a href=\"/wiki/George_Latimer_(New_York_politician)\" title=\"George Latimer (New York politician)\">George Latimer</a>, who won the general election.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-JamaalBowman&#95;66-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-JamaalBowman-66\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>64<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li></ol>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Republicans\">Republicans</h4><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Republicans\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<p>Two Republicans lost renomination.\n</p>\n<ol><li><span data-sort-value=\"Alabama01&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Alabama%27s_1st_congressional_district\" title=\"Alabama&#39;s 1st congressional district\">Alabama&#160;1</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Jerry_Carl\" title=\"Jerry Carl\">Jerry Carl</a> lost a redistricting race to fellow incumbent <a href=\"/wiki/Barry_Moore_(American_politician)\" title=\"Barry Moore (American politician)\">Barry Moore</a>, who won the general election.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-67\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-67\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>65<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Virginia05&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Virginia%27s_5th_congressional_district\" title=\"Virginia&#39;s 5th congressional district\">Virginia&#160;5</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Bob_Good\" title=\"Bob Good\">Bob Good</a> lost renomination to <a href=\"/wiki/John_McGuire_(Virginia_politician)\" title=\"John McGuire (Virginia politician)\">John McGuire</a>, who won the general election.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-Schmidt&#95;68-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Schmidt-68\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>66<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li></ol>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"In_general_elections\">In general elections</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: In general elections\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Democrats\">Democrats</h4><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17\" title=\"Edit section: Democrats\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<p>Four Democrats, one of whom was a freshman, lost re-election to Republicans.\n</p>\n<ol><li><span data-sort-value=\"AlaskaAL&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Alaska%27s_at-large_congressional_district\" title=\"Alaska&#39;s at-large congressional district\">Alaska&#160;at-large</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Mary_Peltola\" title=\"Mary Peltola\">Mary Peltola</a> (first elected in a <a href=\"/wiki/2022_Alaska%27s_at-large_congressional_district_special_election\" title=\"2022 Alaska&#39;s at-large congressional district special election\">2022 special election</a>) lost to <a href=\"/wiki/Nick_Begich_III\" title=\"Nick Begich III\">Nick Begich III</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-69\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-69\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>67<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Colorado08&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Colorado%27s_8th_congressional_district\" title=\"Colorado&#39;s 8th congressional district\">Colorado&#160;8</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Yadira_Caraveo\" title=\"Yadira Caraveo\">Yadira Caraveo</a> (first elected in 2022) lost to <a href=\"/wiki/Gabe_Evans\" title=\"Gabe Evans\">Gabe Evans</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-70\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-70\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>68<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Pennsylvania07&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Pennsylvania%27s_7th_congressional_district\" title=\"Pennsylvania&#39;s 7th congressional district\">Pennsylvania&#160;7</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Susan_Wild\" title=\"Susan Wild\">Susan Wild</a> (first elected in 2018) lost to <a href=\"/wiki/Ryan_Mackenzie\" title=\"Ryan Mackenzie\">Ryan Mackenzie</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-71\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-71\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>69<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Pennsylvania08&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Pennsylvania%27s_8th_congressional_district\" title=\"Pennsylvania&#39;s 8th congressional district\">Pennsylvania&#160;8</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Matt_Cartwright\" title=\"Matt Cartwright\">Matt Cartwright</a> (first elected in 2012) lost to <a href=\"/wiki/Rob_Bresnahan\" title=\"Rob Bresnahan\">Rob Bresnahan</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-72\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-72\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>70<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li></ol>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Republicans_2\">Republicans</h4><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=18\" title=\"Edit section: Republicans\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<p>Seven Republicans, five of whom were freshmen, lost re-election to Democrats.\n</p>\n<ol><li><span data-sort-value=\"California13&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/California%27s_13th_congressional_district\" title=\"California&#39;s 13th congressional district\">California&#160;13</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/John_Duarte_(politician)\" title=\"John Duarte (politician)\">John Duarte</a> (first elected in 2022) lost to <a href=\"/wiki/Adam_Gray\" title=\"Adam Gray\">Adam Gray</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-73\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-73\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>71<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"California27&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/California%27s_27th_congressional_district\" title=\"California&#39;s 27th congressional district\">California&#160;27</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Mike_Garcia_(politician)\" title=\"Mike Garcia (politician)\">Mike Garcia</a> (first elected in 2020) lost to <a href=\"/wiki/George_T._Whitesides\" title=\"George T. Whitesides\">George Whitesides</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-74\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-74\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>72<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/California%27s_45th_congressional_district\" title=\"California&#39;s 45th congressional district\">California 45</a>: <a href=\"/wiki/Michelle_Steel\" title=\"Michelle Steel\">Michelle Steel</a> (first elected in 2020) lost to <a href=\"/wiki/Derek_Tran\" title=\"Derek Tran\">Derek Tran</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-75\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-75\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>73<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"New York04&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/New_York%27s_4th_congressional_district\" title=\"New York&#39;s 4th congressional district\">New York&#160;4</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Anthony_D%27Esposito\" title=\"Anthony D&#39;Esposito\">Anthony D'Esposito</a> (first elected in 2022) lost to <a href=\"/wiki/Laura_Gillen\" title=\"Laura Gillen\">Laura Gillen</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-76\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-76\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>74<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"New York19&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/New_York%27s_19th_congressional_district\" title=\"New York&#39;s 19th congressional district\">New York&#160;19</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Marc_Molinaro\" title=\"Marc Molinaro\">Marc Molinaro</a> (first elected in 2022) lost to <a href=\"/wiki/Josh_Riley\" title=\"Josh Riley\">Josh Riley</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-77\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-77\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>75<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"New York22&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/New_York%27s_22nd_congressional_district\" title=\"New York&#39;s 22nd congressional district\">New York&#160;22</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Brandon_Williams_(politician)\" title=\"Brandon Williams (politician)\">Brandon Williams</a> (first elected in 2022) lost to <a href=\"/wiki/John_Mannion_(American_politician)\" title=\"John Mannion (American politician)\">John Mannion</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-78\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-78\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>76<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Oregon05&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Oregon%27s_5th_congressional_district\" title=\"Oregon&#39;s 5th congressional district\">Oregon&#160;5</a></span>: <a href=\"/wiki/Lori_Chavez-DeRemer\" title=\"Lori Chavez-DeRemer\">Lori Chavez-DeRemer</a> (first elected in 2022) lost to <a href=\"/wiki/Janelle_Bynum\" title=\"Janelle Bynum\">Janelle Bynum</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-79\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-79\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>77<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li></ol>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Open_seats_that_changed_parties\">Open seats that changed parties</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=19\" title=\"Edit section: Open seats that changed parties\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r1216972533\">.mw-parser-output .col-begin{border-collapse:collapse;padding:0;color:inherit;width:100%;border:0;margin:0}.mw-parser-output .col-begin-small{font-size:90%}.mw-parser-output .col-break{vertical-align:top;text-align:left}.mw-parser-output .col-break-2{width:50%}.mw-parser-output .col-break-3{width:33.3%}.mw-parser-output .col-break-4{width:25%}.mw-parser-output .col-break-5{width:20%}@media(max-width:720px){.mw-parser-output .col-begin,.mw-parser-output .col-begin>tbody,.mw-parser-output .col-begin>tbody>tr,.mw-parser-output .col-begin>tbody>tr>td{display:block!important;width:100%!important}.mw-parser-output .col-break{padding-left:0!important}}</style><div>\n<table class=\"col-begin\" role=\"presentation\">\n\n\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td class=\"col-break\">\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Republican_seats_won_by_Democrats\">Republican seats won by Democrats</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=20\" title=\"Edit section: Republican seats won by Democrats\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<p>Three Republican seats were won by Democrats.\n</p>\n<ol><li><span data-sort-value=\"Alabama02&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Alabama%27s_2nd_congressional_district\" title=\"Alabama&#39;s 2nd congressional district\">Alabama&#160;2</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Shomari_Figures\" title=\"Shomari Figures\">Shomari Figures</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Louisiana06&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Louisiana%27s_6th_congressional_district\" title=\"Louisiana&#39;s 6th congressional district\">Louisiana&#160;6</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Cleo_Fields\" title=\"Cleo Fields\">Cleo Fields</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-80\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-80\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>78<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Puerto RicoAL&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Puerto_Rico%27s_at-large_congressional_district\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Puerto Rico&#39;s at-large congressional district\">Puerto Rico&#160;at-large</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Pablo_Hern%C3%A1ndez_Rivera\" title=\"Pablo Hernández Rivera\">Pablo Hernández Rivera</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-81\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-81\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>79<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li></ol>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n</td>\n<td class=\"col-break\">\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Democratic_seats_won_by_Republicans\">Democratic seats won by Republicans</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=21\" title=\"Edit section: Democratic seats won by Republicans\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<p>Five Democratic seats were won by Republicans.\n</p>\n<ol><li><span data-sort-value=\"Michigan07&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Michigan%27s_7th_congressional_district\" title=\"Michigan&#39;s 7th congressional district\">Michigan&#160;7</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Tom_Barrett_(Michigan_politician)\" title=\"Tom Barrett (Michigan politician)\">Tom Barrett</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-82\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-82\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>80<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"North Carolina06&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/North_Carolina%27s_6th_congressional_district\" title=\"North Carolina&#39;s 6th congressional district\">North Carolina&#160;6</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Addison_McDowell\" title=\"Addison McDowell\">Addison McDowell</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-83\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-83\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>81<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"North Carolina13&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/North_Carolina%27s_13th_congressional_district\" title=\"North Carolina&#39;s 13th congressional district\">North Carolina&#160;13</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Brad_Knott\" title=\"Brad Knott\">Brad Knott</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-84\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-84\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>82<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"North Carolina14&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/North_Carolina%27s_14th_congressional_district\" title=\"North Carolina&#39;s 14th congressional district\">North Carolina&#160;14</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Tim_Moore_(North_Carolina_politician)\" title=\"Tim Moore (North Carolina politician)\">Tim Moore</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-85\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-85\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>83<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Northern Mariana IslandsAL&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Northern_Mariana_Islands%27_at-large_congressional_district\" title=\"Northern Mariana Islands&#39; at-large congressional district\">Northern Mariana Islands&#160;at-large</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Kimberlyn_King-Hinds\" title=\"Kimberlyn King-Hinds\">Kimberlyn King-Hinds</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-86\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-86\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>84<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li></ol>\n<p>&#32;\n</p>\n</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Open_seats_that_parties_held\">Open seats that parties held</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=22\" title=\"Edit section: Open seats that parties held\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1216972533\" /><div>\n<table class=\"col-begin\" role=\"presentation\">\n\n\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td class=\"col-break\">\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Democratic_seats_held_by_Democrats\">Democratic seats held by Democrats</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=23\" title=\"Edit section: Democratic seats held by Democrats\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<p>Democrats held twenty-four of their open seats.\n</p>\n<ol><li><span data-sort-value=\"Arizona03&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Arizona%27s_3rd_congressional_district\" title=\"Arizona&#39;s 3rd congressional district\">Arizona&#160;3</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Yassamin_Ansari\" title=\"Yassamin Ansari\">Yassamin Ansari</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"California12&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/California%27s_12th_congressional_district\" title=\"California&#39;s 12th congressional district\">California&#160;12</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Lateefah_Simon\" title=\"Lateefah Simon\">Lateefah Simon</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"California16&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/California%27s_16th_congressional_district\" title=\"California&#39;s 16th congressional district\">California&#160;16</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Sam_Liccardo\" title=\"Sam Liccardo\">Sam Liccardo</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"California29&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/California%27s_29th_congressional_district\" title=\"California&#39;s 29th congressional district\">California&#160;29</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Luz_Rivas\" title=\"Luz Rivas\">Luz Rivas</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"California30&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/California%27s_30th_congressional_district\" title=\"California&#39;s 30th congressional district\">California&#160;30</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Laura_Friedman\" title=\"Laura Friedman\">Laura Friedman</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"California31&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/California%27s_31st_congressional_district\" title=\"California&#39;s 31st congressional district\">California&#160;31</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Gil_Cisneros\" title=\"Gil Cisneros\">Gil Cisneros</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"California47&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/California%27s_47th_congressional_district\" title=\"California&#39;s 47th congressional district\">California&#160;47</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Dave_Min\" title=\"Dave Min\">Dave Min</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"DelawareAL&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Delaware%27s_at-large_congressional_district\" title=\"Delaware&#39;s at-large congressional district\">Delaware&#160;at-large</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Sarah_McBride\" title=\"Sarah McBride\">Sarah McBride</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Maryland02&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Maryland%27s_2nd_congressional_district\" title=\"Maryland&#39;s 2nd congressional district\">Maryland&#160;2</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Johnny_Olszewski\" title=\"Johnny Olszewski\">Johnny Olszewski</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Maryland03&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Maryland%27s_3rd_congressional_district\" title=\"Maryland&#39;s 3rd congressional district\">Maryland&#160;3</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Sarah_Elfreth\" title=\"Sarah Elfreth\">Sarah Elfreth</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Maryland06&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Maryland%27s_6th_congressional_district\" title=\"Maryland&#39;s 6th congressional district\">Maryland&#160;6</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/April_McClain_Delaney\" title=\"April McClain Delaney\">April McClain Delaney</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Michigan08&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Michigan%27s_8th_congressional_district\" title=\"Michigan&#39;s 8th congressional district\">Michigan&#160;8</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Kristen_McDonald_Rivet\" title=\"Kristen McDonald Rivet\">Kristen McDonald Rivet</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Minnesota03&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Minnesota%27s_3rd_congressional_district\" title=\"Minnesota&#39;s 3rd congressional district\">Minnesota&#160;3</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Kelly_Morrison\" title=\"Kelly Morrison\">Kelly Morrison</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Missouri01&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Missouri%27s_1st_congressional_district\" title=\"Missouri&#39;s 1st congressional district\">Missouri&#160;1</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Wesley_Bell\" title=\"Wesley Bell\">Wesley Bell</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"New Hampshire02&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/New_Hampshire%27s_2nd_congressional_district\" title=\"New Hampshire&#39;s 2nd congressional district\">New Hampshire&#160;2</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Maggie_Goodlander\" title=\"Maggie Goodlander\">Maggie Goodlander</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"New Jersey03&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/New_Jersey%27s_3rd_congressional_district\" title=\"New Jersey&#39;s 3rd congressional district\">New Jersey&#160;3</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Herb_Conaway\" title=\"Herb Conaway\">Herb Conaway</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"New Jersey09&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/New_Jersey%27s_9th_congressional_district\" title=\"New Jersey&#39;s 9th congressional district\">New Jersey&#160;9</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Nellie_Pou\" title=\"Nellie Pou\">Nellie Pou</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"New York16&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/New_York%27s_16th_congressional_district\" title=\"New York&#39;s 16th congressional district\">New York&#160;16</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/George_Latimer_(New_York_politician)\" title=\"George Latimer (New York politician)\">George Latimer</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Oregon03&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Oregon%27s_3rd_congressional_district\" title=\"Oregon&#39;s 3rd congressional district\">Oregon&#160;3</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Maxine_Dexter\" title=\"Maxine Dexter\">Maxine Dexter</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Texas18&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Texas%27s_18th_congressional_district\" title=\"Texas&#39;s 18th congressional district\">Texas&#160;18</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Sylvester_Turner\" title=\"Sylvester Turner\">Sylvester Turner</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Texas32&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Texas%27s_32nd_congressional_district\" title=\"Texas&#39;s 32nd congressional district\">Texas&#160;32</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Julie_Johnson_(politician)\" title=\"Julie Johnson (politician)\">Julie Johnson</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Virginia07&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Virginia%27s_7th_congressional_district\" title=\"Virginia&#39;s 7th congressional district\">Virginia&#160;7</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Eugene_Vindman\" title=\"Eugene Vindman\">Eugene Vindman</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Virginia10&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Virginia%27s_10th_congressional_district\" title=\"Virginia&#39;s 10th congressional district\">Virginia&#160;10</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Suhas_Subramanyam\" title=\"Suhas Subramanyam\">Suhas Subramanyam</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Washington06&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Washington%27s_6th_congressional_district\" title=\"Washington&#39;s 6th congressional district\">Washington&#160;6</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Emily_Randall\" title=\"Emily Randall\">Emily Randall</a>.</li></ol>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n</td>\n<td class=\"col-break\">\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Republican_seats_held_by_Republicans\">Republican seats held by Republicans</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=24\" title=\"Edit section: Republican seats held by Republicans\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<p>Republicans held twenty-three of their open seats.\n</p>\n<ol><li><span data-sort-value=\"Arizona08&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Arizona%27s_8th_congressional_district\" title=\"Arizona&#39;s 8th congressional district\">Arizona&#160;8</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Abraham_Hamadeh\" title=\"Abraham Hamadeh\">Abraham Hamadeh</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Colorado03&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Colorado%27s_3rd_congressional_district\" title=\"Colorado&#39;s 3rd congressional district\">Colorado&#160;3</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Jeff_Hurd_(politician)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Jeff Hurd (politician)\">Jeff Hurd</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Colorado05&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Colorado%27s_5th_congressional_district\" title=\"Colorado&#39;s 5th congressional district\">Colorado&#160;5</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Jeff_Crank\" title=\"Jeff Crank\">Jeff Crank</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Florida08&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Florida%27s_8th_congressional_district\" title=\"Florida&#39;s 8th congressional district\">Florida&#160;8</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Mike_Haridopolos\" title=\"Mike Haridopolos\">Mike Haridopolos</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Georgia03&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Georgia%27s_3rd_congressional_district\" title=\"Georgia&#39;s 3rd congressional district\">Georgia&#160;3</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Brian_Jack\" title=\"Brian Jack\">Brian Jack</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Indiana03&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Indiana%27s_3rd_congressional_district\" title=\"Indiana&#39;s 3rd congressional district\">Indiana&#160;3</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Marlin_Stutzman\" title=\"Marlin Stutzman\">Marlin Stutzman</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Indiana06&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Indiana%27s_6th_congressional_district\" title=\"Indiana&#39;s 6th congressional district\">Indiana&#160;6</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Jefferson_Shreve\" title=\"Jefferson Shreve\">Jefferson Shreve</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Indiana08&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Indiana%27s_8th_congressional_district\" title=\"Indiana&#39;s 8th congressional district\">Indiana&#160;8</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Mark_Messmer\" title=\"Mark Messmer\">Mark Messmer</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Kansas02&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Kansas%27s_2nd_congressional_district\" title=\"Kansas&#39;s 2nd congressional district\">Kansas&#160;2</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Derek_Schmidt\" title=\"Derek Schmidt\">Derek Schmidt</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Missouri03&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Missouri%27s_3rd_congressional_district\" title=\"Missouri&#39;s 3rd congressional district\">Missouri&#160;3</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Bob_Onder\" title=\"Bob Onder\">Bob Onder</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Montana02&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Montana%27s_2nd_congressional_district\" title=\"Montana&#39;s 2nd congressional district\">Montana&#160;2</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Troy_Downing\" title=\"Troy Downing\">Troy Downing</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"North Carolina08&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/North_Carolina%27s_8th_congressional_district\" title=\"North Carolina&#39;s 8th congressional district\">North Carolina&#160;8</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Mark_Harris_(North_Carolina_politician)\" title=\"Mark Harris (North Carolina politician)\">Mark Harris</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"North Carolina10&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/North_Carolina%27s_10th_congressional_district\" title=\"North Carolina&#39;s 10th congressional district\">North Carolina&#160;10</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Pat_Harrigan\" title=\"Pat Harrigan\">Pat Harrigan</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"North DakotaAL&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/North_Dakota%27s_at-large_congressional_district\" title=\"North Dakota&#39;s at-large congressional district\">North Dakota&#160;at-large</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Julie_Fedorchak\" title=\"Julie Fedorchak\">Julie Fedorchak</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Ohio02&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Ohio%27s_2nd_congressional_district\" title=\"Ohio&#39;s 2nd congressional district\">Ohio&#160;2</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/David_Taylor_(Ohio_politician)\" title=\"David Taylor (Ohio politician)\">David Taylor</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"South Carolina03&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/South_Carolina%27s_3rd_congressional_district\" title=\"South Carolina&#39;s 3rd congressional district\">South Carolina&#160;3</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Sheri_Biggs\" title=\"Sheri Biggs\">Sheri Biggs</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Texas12&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Texas%27s_12th_congressional_district\" title=\"Texas&#39;s 12th congressional district\">Texas&#160;12</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Craig_Goldman\" title=\"Craig Goldman\">Craig Goldman</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Texas26&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Texas%27s_26th_congressional_district\" title=\"Texas&#39;s 26th congressional district\">Texas&#160;26</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Brandon_Gill\" title=\"Brandon Gill\">Brandon Gill</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Utah03&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Utah%27s_3rd_congressional_district\" title=\"Utah&#39;s 3rd congressional district\">Utah&#160;3</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Mike_Kennedy\" title=\"Mike Kennedy\">Mike Kennedy</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Virginia05&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Virginia%27s_5th_congressional_district\" title=\"Virginia&#39;s 5th congressional district\">Virginia&#160;5</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/John_McGuire_(Virginia_politician)\" title=\"John McGuire (Virginia politician)\">John McGuire</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Washington05&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Washington%27s_5th_congressional_district\" title=\"Washington&#39;s 5th congressional district\">Washington&#160;5</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Michael_Baumgartner\" title=\"Michael Baumgartner\">Michael Baumgartner</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"West Virginia02&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/West_Virginia%27s_2nd_congressional_district\" title=\"West Virginia&#39;s 2nd congressional district\">West Virginia&#160;2</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Riley_Moore\" title=\"Riley Moore\">Riley Moore</a>.</li>\n<li><span data-sort-value=\"Wisconsin08&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Wisconsin%27s_8th_congressional_district\" title=\"Wisconsin&#39;s 8th congressional district\">Wisconsin&#160;8</a></span>: Won by <a href=\"/wiki/Tony_Wied\" title=\"Tony Wied\">Tony Wied</a>, who also won the district's special election.</li></ol>\n<p>&#32;\n</p>\n</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Crossover_seats\">Crossover seats</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=25\" title=\"Edit section: Crossover seats\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<p>This is a list of congressional seats that voted for one party in the <a href=\"/wiki/2020_United_States_presidential_election\" title=\"2020 United States presidential election\">2020 presidential election</a> and another in the <a href=\"/wiki/2022_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections\" title=\"2022 United States House of Representatives elections\">2022 House elections</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-87\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-87\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>85<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Democratic_4\">Democratic</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=26\" title=\"Edit section: Democratic\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<p>This lists the districts in which <a href=\"/wiki/Donald_Trump\" title=\"Donald Trump\">Donald Trump</a> won in 2020 that were represented by Democrats:\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th colspan=\"3\">District\n</th>\n<th colspan=\"5\">Incumbent\n</th></tr>\n<tr valign=\"bottom\">\n<th>Location\n</th>\n<th><a href=\"/wiki/Cook_Partisan_Voting_Index\" title=\"Cook Partisan Voting Index\">2022<br />PVI</a><sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-new&#95;pvi&#95;88-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-new_pvi-88\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>86<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</th>\n<th>Trump margin of<br />victory in 2020\n</th>\n<th>Member\n</th>\n<th>Party\n</th>\n<th>First<br />elected\n</th>\n<th>Incumbent margin<br />of victory in 2022\n</th>\n<th>Result\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span data-sort-value=\"AlaskaAL&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Alaska%27s_at-large_congressional_district\" title=\"Alaska&#39;s at-large congressional district\">Alaska&#160;at-large</a></span>\n</th>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\"><span data-sort-value=\"108&#160;!\">R+8</span>\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\"><span data-sort-value=\"110.1&#160;!\">R+10.1</span>\n</td>\n<td><span data-sort-value=\"Peltola, Mary\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Mary_Peltola\" title=\"Mary Peltola\">Mary Peltola</a></span></span></span>\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\">Democratic\n</td>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/2022_Alaska%27s_at-large_congressional_district_special_election\" title=\"2022 Alaska&#39;s at-large congressional district special election\">2022 <span style=\"font-size: 85%;\">(special)</span></a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\"><span data-sort-value=\"90.1&#160;!\">D+9.9</span>\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\" data-sort-value=\"1\"><a href=\"/wiki/Nick_Begich_III\" title=\"Nick Begich III\">Begich</a> <small>(flip)</small>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span data-sort-value=\"Maine02&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Maine%27s_2nd_congressional_district\" title=\"Maine&#39;s 2nd congressional district\">Maine&#160;2</a></span>\n</th>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\"><span data-s