CEFF\">Democratic\n</td>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/2012_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_Pennsylvania#District_17\" title=\"2012 United States House of Representatives elections in Pennsylvania\">2012</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\"><span data-sort-value=\"97.6&#160;!\">D+2.4</span>\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\" data-sort-value=\"1\"><a href=\"/wiki/Rob_Bresnahan\" title=\"Rob Bresnahan\">Bresnahan</a> <small>(flip)</small>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span data-sort-value=\"Washington03&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Washington%27s_3rd_congressional_district\" title=\"Washington&#39;s 3rd congressional district\">Washington&#160;3</a></span>\n</th>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\"><span data-sort-value=\"105&#160;!\">R+5</span>\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\"><span data-sort-value=\"104.2&#160;!\">R+4.2</span>\n</td>\n<td><span data-sort-value=\"Gluesenkamp Perez, Marie\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Marie_Gluesenkamp_Perez\" title=\"Marie Gluesenkamp Perez\">Marie Gluesenkamp Perez</a></span></span></span>\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\">Democratic\n</td>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/2022_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_Washington#District_3\" title=\"2022 United States House of Representatives elections in Washington\">2022</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\"><span data-sort-value=\"99.2&#160;!\">D+0.8</span>\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\" data-sort-value=\"-1\">Gluesenkamp Perez\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Republican_3\">Republican</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=27\" title=\"Edit section: Republican\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<p>This lists the districts in which <a href=\"/wiki/Joe_Biden\" title=\"Joe Biden\">Joe Biden</a> won in 2020 that were represented by Republican:\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th colspan=\"3\">District\n</th>\n<th colspan=\"5\">Incumbent\n</th></tr>\n<tr valign=\"bottom\">\n<th>Location\n</th>\n<th><a href=\"/wiki/Cook_Partisan_Voting_Index\" title=\"Cook Partisan Voting Index\">2022<br />PVI</a><sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-new&#95;pvi&#95;88-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-new_pvi-88\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>86<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</th>\n<th>Biden margin of<br />victory in 2020\n</th>\n<th>Member\n</th>\n<th>Party\n</th>\n<th>First<br />elected\n</th>\n<th>Incumbent margin<br />of victory in 2022\n</th>\n<th>Result\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span data-sort-value=\"Alabama02&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Alabama%27s_2nd_congressional_district\" title=\"Alabama&#39;s 2nd congressional district\">Alabama&#160;2</a></span>\n</th>\n<td style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\"><span data-sort-value=\"96&#160;!\">D+4</span><sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-Redistrict&#95;89-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Redistrict-89\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>c<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\"><span data-sort-value=\"87.6&#160;!\">D+12.4</span>\n</td>\n<td><span data-sort-value=\"Moore, Barry\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Barry_Moore_(American_politician)\" title=\"Barry Moore (American politician)\">Barry Moore</a></span></span></span><sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-Moore&#95;93-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Moore-93\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>g<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><br /><small>(running in the 1st district)</small>\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB