/a></span>\n</th>\n<td data-sort-value=\"1\" style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\">Democratic\n</td>\n<td>8.09%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span data-sort-value=\"Washington08&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Washington%27s_8th_congressional_district\" title=\"Washington&#39;s 8th congressional district\">Washington&#160;8th</a></span>\n</th>\n<td data-sort-value=\"1\" style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\">Democratic\n</td>\n<td>8.17%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span data-sort-value=\"Illinois06&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Illinois%27s_6th_congressional_district\" title=\"Illinois&#39;s 6th congressional district\">Illinois&#160;6th</a></span>\n</th>\n<td data-sort-value=\"1\" style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\">Democratic\n</td>\n<td>8.42%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span data-sort-value=\"Indiana01&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Indiana%27s_1st_congressional_district\" title=\"Indiana&#39;s 1st congressional district\">Indiana&#160;1st</a></span>\n</th>\n<td data-sort-value=\"1\" style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\">Democratic\n</td>\n<td>8.49%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span data-sort-value=\"New Jersey03&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/New_Jersey%27s_3rd_congressional_district\" title=\"New Jersey&#39;s 3rd congressional district\">New Jersey&#160;3rd</a></span>\n</th>\n<td data-sort-value=\"1\" style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\">Democratic\n</td>\n<td>8.59%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span data-sort-value=\"Illinois17&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Illinois%27s_17th_congressional_district\" title=\"Illinois&#39;s 17th congressional district\">Illinois&#160;17th</a></span>\n</th>\n<td data-sort-value=\"1\" style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\">Democratic\n</td>\n<td>8.85%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span data-sort-value=\"Florida25&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Florida%27s_25th_congressional_district\" title=\"Florida&#39;s 25th congressional district\">Florida&#160;25th</a></span>\n</th>\n<td data-sort-value=\"1\" style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\">Democratic\n</td>\n<td>8.96%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span data-sort-value=\"Arizona02&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Arizona%27s_2nd_congressional_district\" title=\"Arizona&#39;s 2nd congressional district\">Arizona&#160;2nd</a></span>\n</th>\n<td data-sort-value=\"1\" style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\">Republican\n</td>\n<td>8.97%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span data-sort-value=\"New York22&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/New_York%27s_22nd_congressional_district\" title=\"New York&#39;s 22nd congressional district\">New York&#160;22nd</a></span>\n</th>\n<td data-sort-value=\"1\" style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\">Democratic (flip)\n</td>\n<td>9.12%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span data-sort-value=\"Ohio01&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Ohio%27s_1st_congressional_district\" title=\"Ohio&#39;s 1st congressional district\">Ohio&#160;1st</a></span>\n</th>\n<td data-sort-value=\"1\" style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\">Democratic\n</td>\n<td>9.17%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span data-sort-value=\"Alabama02&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Alabama%27s_2nd_congressional_district\" title=\"Alabama&#39;s 2nd congressional district\">Alabama&#160;2nd</a></span>\n</th>\n<td data-sort-value=\"1\" style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\">Democratic (flip)\n</td>\n<td>9.20%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span data-sort-value=\"Florida13&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Florida%27s_13th_congressional_district\" title=\"Florida&#39;s 13th congressional district\">Florida&#160;13th</a></span>\n</th>\n<td data-sort-value=\"1\" style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\">Republican\n</td>\n<td>9.65%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span data-sort-value=\"Michigan03&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Michigan%27s_3rd_congressional_district\" title=\"Michigan&#39;s 3rd congressional district\">Michigan&#160;3rd</a></span>\n</th>\n<td data-sort-value=\"1\" style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\">Democratic\n</td>\n<td>9.89%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span data-sort-value=\"Florida22&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Florida%27s_22nd_congressional_district\" title=\"Florida&#39;s 22nd congressional district\">Florida&#160;22nd</a></span>\n</th>\n<td data-sort-value=\"1\" style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\">Democratic\n</td>\n<td>9.91%\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Election_ratings\">Election ratings</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=32\" title=\"Edit section: Election ratings\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" /><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_election_ratings\" title=\"2024 United States House of Representatives election ratings\">2024 United States House of Representatives election ratings</a></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Special_elections\">Special elections</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=33\" title=\"Edit section: Special elections\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" /><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">See also: <a href=\"/wiki/List_of_special_elections_to_the_United_States_House_of_Representatives\" title=\"List of special elections to the United States House of Representatives\">List of special elections to the United States House of Representatives</a></div>\n<p>There were eight special elections scheduled in 2024 to the <a href=\"/wiki/118th_United_States_Congress\" title=\"118th United States Congress\">118th United States Congress</a>, listed here by date and district.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable\">\n\n\n<tbody><tr valign=\"bottom\">\n<th rowspan=\"2\">District\n</th>\n<th colspan=\"3\">Incumbent\n</th>\n<th colspan=\"2\">This race\n</th></tr>\n\n<tr valign=\"bottom\">\n<th>Member\n</th>\n<th>Party\n</th>\n<th>First elected\n</th>\n<th class=\"unsortable\" data-sort-type=\"date\">Results\n</th>\n<th class=\"unsortable\">Candidates\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span data-sort-value=\"New York03&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/New_York%27s_3rd_congressional_district\" title=\"New York&#39;s 3rd congressional district\">New York&#160;3</a></span>\n</th>\n<td><span data-sort-value=\"Santos, George\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/George_Santos\" title=\"George Santos\">George Santos</a></span></span></span>\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\">Republican\n</td>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/2022_New_York%27s_3rd_congressional_district_election\" title=\"2022 New York&#39;s 3rd congressional district election\">2022</a>\n</td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"February\" style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\">Incumbent <a href=\"/wiki/George_Santos#Expulsion_resolutions\" title=\"George Santos\">expelled</a> December 1, 2023.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-SantosNY&#95;139-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SantosNY-139\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>128<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><br />New member <a href=\"/wiki/2024_New_York%27s_3rd_congressional_district_special_election\" title=\"2024 New York&#39;s 3rd congressional district special election\">elected</a> February 13, 2024.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-NY-03&#95;sp&#95;140-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-NY-03_sp-140\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>129<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><br /><b>Democratic gain.</b>\n</td>\n<td nowrap=\"\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r1126788409\">.mw-parser-output .plainlist ol,.mw-parser-output .plainlist ul{line-height:inherit;list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}.mw-parser-output .plainlist ol li,.mw-parser-output .plainlist ul li{margin-bottom:0}</style><div class=\"plainlist\">\n<ul><li><span style=\"color: #0044C9;\">▌</span><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img alt=\"Green tick\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Green_check.svg/20px-Green_check.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Green_check.svg/40px-Green_check.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"600\" data-file-height=\"600\" /></span></span><span style=\"display:none\">Y</span> <b><span data-sort-value=\"Suozzi, Tom\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Tom_Suozzi\" title=\"Tom Suozzi\">Tom Suozzi</a></span></span></span></b> (Democratic) 53.9%</li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #E81B23;\">▌</span><a href=\"/wiki/Mazi_Melesa_Pilip\" title=\"Mazi Melesa Pilip\">Mazi Melesa Pilip</a> (Republican) 45.9%<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-Results-NY03&#95;141-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Results-NY03-141\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>130<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n</div>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span data-sort-value=\"New York26&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/New_York%27s_26th_congressional_district\" title=\"New York&#39;s 26th congressional district\">New York&#160;26</a></span>\n</th>\n<td><span data-sort-value=\"Higgins, Brian\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Brian_Higgins\" title=\"Brian Higgins\">Brian Higgins</a></span></span></span>\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black;background-color:#B0CEFF\">Democratic\n</td>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/2004_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_New_York\" title=\"2004 United States House of Representatives elections in New York\">2004</a>\n</td>\n<td data-sort-value=\"April\" style=\"background:#EEF6FF\">Incumbent resigned February 2, 2024.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-HigginsNY&#95;142-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-HigginsNY-142\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>131<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><br />New member <a href=\"/wiki/2024_New_York%27s_26th_congressional_district_special_election\" title=\"2024 New York&#39;s 26th congressional district special election\">elected</a> April 30, 2024.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-NY-26&#95;sp&#95;143-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-NY-26_sp-143\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>132<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><br />Democratic hold.\n</td>\n<td nowrap=\"\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1126788409\" /><div class=\"plainlist\">\n<ul><li><span style=\"color: #0044C9;\">▌</span><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img alt=\"Green tick\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Green_check.svg/20px-Green_check.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Green_check.svg/40px-Green_check.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"600\" data-file-height=\"600\" /></span></span><span style=\"display:none\">Y</span> <b><span data-sort-value=\"Kennedy, Tim\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Tim_Kennedy_(politician)\" title=\"Tim Kennedy (politician)\">Tim Kennedy</a></span></span></span></b> (Democratic) 68.5%</li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #E81B23;\">▌</span>Gary Dickson (Republican) 31.3%<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-Results-NY26&#95;144-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Results-NY26-144\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>133<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n</div>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span data-sort-value=\"California20&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/California%27s_20th_congressional_district\" title=\"California&#39;s 20th congressional district\">California&#160;20</a></span>\n</th>\n<td><span data-sort-value=\"McCarthy, Kevin\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Kevin_McCarthy\" title=\"Kevin McCarthy\">Kevin McCarthy</a></span></span></span>\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\">Republican\n</td>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/2006_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_California\" title=\"2006 United States House of Representatives elections in California\">2006</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"background:#FFF1EE\">Incumbent resigned December 31, 2023.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-McCarthy&#95;145-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-McCarthy-145\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>134<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><br />New member <a href=\"/wiki/2024_California%27s_20th_congressional_district_special_election\" title=\"2024 California&#39;s 20th congressional district special election\">elected</a> May 21, 2024, after no candidate<br />won a majority in the March 19 jungle primary.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-146\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-146\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>135<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><br />Republican hold.\n</td>\n<td nowrap=\"\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1126788409\" /><div class=\"plainlist\">\n<ul><li><span style=\"color: #E81B23;\">▌</span><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img alt=\"Green tick\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Green_check.svg/20px-Green_check.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Green_check.svg/40px-Green_check.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"600\" data-file-height=\"600\" /></span></span><span style=\"display:none\">Y</span> <b><span data-sort-value=\"Fong, Vince\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Vince_Fong\" title=\"Vince Fong\">Vince Fong</a></span></span></span></b> (Republican) 60.6%</li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #E81B23;\">▌</span>Mike Boudreaux (Republican) 39.4%<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-Results-CA20&#95;147-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Results-CA20-147\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>136<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n</div>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th><span data-sort-value=\"Ohio06&#160;!\"><a href=\"/wiki/Ohio%27s_6th_congressional_district\" title=\"Ohio&#39;s 6th congressional district\">Ohio&#160;6</a></span>\n</th>\n<td><span data-sort-value=\"Johnson, Bill\"><span class=\"vcard\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Bill_Johnson_(Ohio_politician)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Bill Johnson (Ohio politician)\">Bill Johnson</a></span></span></span>\n</td>\n<td style=\"color:black; background-color:#FFB6B6\">Republican\n</td>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/2010_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_Ohio#District_6\" title=\"2010 United States House of Representatives elections in Ohio\">2010</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"background:#FFF1EE\">Incumbent resigned January 21, 2024.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-JohnsonOH2&#95;148-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-JohnsonOH2-148\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>137<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><br />New member <a href=\"/wiki/2024_Ohio%27s_6th_congressional_district_special_election\" title=\"2024 Ohio&#39;s 6th congressional district special election\">electe