tyles:r1333433106\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFMcCaskill2022\" class=\"citation web cs1\">McCaskill, Nolan D. (November 30, 2022). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20221130195253/https://www.latimes.com/politics/story/2022-11-30/house-democrats-elect-jeffries-as-congress-first-black-party-leader\">\"House Democrats elect Hakeem Jeffries as Congress' first black party leader\"</a>. <i><a href=\"/wiki/Los_Angeles_Times\" title=\"Los Angeles Times\">Los Angeles Times</a></i>. <a href=\"/wiki/Washington,_D.C.\" title=\"Washington, D.C.\">Washington</a>. Archived from <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.latimes.com/politics/story/2022-11-30/house-democrats-elect-jeffries-as-congress-first-black-party-leader\">the original</a> on November 30, 2022<span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">December 1,</span> 2022</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=Los+Angeles+Times&amp;rft.atitle=House+Democrats+elect+Hakeem+Jeffries+as+Congress%27+first+black+party+leader&amp;rft.date=2022-11-30&amp;rft.aulast=McCaskill&amp;rft.aufirst=Nolan+D.&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.latimes.com%2Fpolitics%2Fstory%2F2022-11-30%2Fhouse-democrats-elect-jeffries-as-congress-first-black-party-leader&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2024+United+States+House+of+Representatives+elections\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-5\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-5\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite class=\"citation web cs1\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20240206045000/https://www.270towin.com/2024-house-election/consensus-2024-house-forecast\">\"2024 House Election: Consensus Forecast\"</a>. <i><a href=\"/wiki/270toWin\" title=\"270toWin\">270toWin</a></i>. Archived from <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.270towin.com/2024-house-election/consensus-2024-house-forecast\">the original</a> on February 6, 2024<span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">February 5,</span> 2024</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=270toWin&amp;rft.atitle=2024+House+Election%3A+Consensus+Forecast&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.270towin.com%2F2024-house-election%2Fconsensus-2024-house-forecast&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2024+United+States+House+of+Representatives+elections\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-6\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-6\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite class=\"citation web cs1\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://history.house.gov/Institution/Party-Divisions/Party-Divisions/\">\"Party Divisions of the House of Representatives, 1789 to Present\"</a>. <i>US House of Representatives: History, Art &amp; Archives</i><span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">December 4,</span> 2024</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=US+House+of+Representatives%3A+History%2C+Art+%26+Archives&amp;rft.atitle=Party+Divisions+of+the+House+of+Representatives%2C+1789+to+Present&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fhistory.house.gov%2FInstitution%2FParty-Divisions%2FParty-Divisions%2F&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2024+United+States+House+of+Representatives+elections\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-7\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-7\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite class=\"citation web cs1\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-elections/house-results\">\"2024 House Results: Republicans keep control\"</a>. <i>NBC News</i>. November 13, 2024<span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">November 13,</span> 2024</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=NBC+News&amp;rft.atitle=2024+House+Results%3A+Republicans+keep+control&amp;rft.date=2024-11-13&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nbcnews.com%2Fpolitics%2F2024-elections%2Fhouse-results&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2024+United+States+House+of+Representatives+elections\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-9\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-9\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFWasserman2024\" class=\"citation web cs1\">Wasserman, Dave [@Redistrict] (December 10, 2024). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://x.com/Redistrict/status/1866528527287292405\">\"Fact: in 2024, the House majority was decided by just 7,309 votes across three districts (#IA01, #CO08 and #PA07) out of 148 million votes cast nationwide\"</a> (<a href=\"/wiki/Tweet_(social_media)\" title=\"Tweet (social media)\">Tweet</a>)<span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">December 13,</span> 2024</span> &#8211; via <a href=\"/wiki/X_(formerly_Twitter)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"X (formerly Twitter)\">X (formerly Twitter)</a>.</cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=Fact%3A+in+2024%2C+the+House+majority+was+decided+by+just+7%2C309+votes+across+three+districts+%28%23IA01%2C+%23CO08+and+%23PA07%29+out+of+148+million+votes+cast+nationwide.&amp;rft.date=2024-12-10&amp;rft.aulast=Wasserman&amp;rft.aufirst=Dave&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fx.com%2FRedistrict%2Fstatus%2F1866528527287292405&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2024+United+States+House+of+Representatives+elections\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-10\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-10\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite class=\"citation web cs1\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://apnews.com/article/pennsylvania-congress-2024-election-perry-mackenzie-bresnahan-3c79f724690fb734cdcc921512165b72\">\"GOP flips 2 US House seats in Pennsylvania, as Republican Scott Perry wins again\"</a>. <i><a href=\"/wiki/Associated_Press_News\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Associated Press News\">Associated Press News</a></i>. November 7, 2024<span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">November 8,</span> 2024</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=Associated+Press+News&amp;rft.atitle=GOP+flips+2+US+House+seats+in+Pennsylvania%2C+as+Republican+Scott+Perry+wins+again&amp;rft.date=2024-11-07&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fapnews.com%2Farticle%2Fpennsylvania-congress-2024-election-perry-mackenzie-bresnahan-3c79f724690fb734cdcc921512165b72&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2024+United+States+House+of+Representatives+elections\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-11\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-11\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"refer